{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact package/builder-room design draft8 at44374d29f2f1f5e5f6e3417d35ac3d1a43279d54, tree446b3c0ca35d9181560c030300e02b63dd075dac. No remaining material findings on this design.\n\nImplementation fidelity: Read the complete676-line primary first, followed by the exact draft7-to8 delta and the cited native result/subject-binding boundaries. Verified all2189 regular Git leaves/blob IDs/modes in separate scratch. Against authored base32b32fc2dd67581b6144520d60e71489ec6b0d22/treeb7362d1e11a68a4f7585a877113f6a196d81de2a, only this note changes and2188 leaves are unchanged. Whitespace check passes. The delivery remains a design for the semantic declarations, validator, authoring forms, staged checks and builder-room configuration, not their runtime implementation.\n\nCorrectness and verification: F1 of f119c3b9 is answered by the restricted successful-slot rule: an opening row makes one creation; any final transition of its creating type may occur only in that creation's refused clause, whose effects name only its exact own on item; conflict enters no final state. Thus one failure cannot retire a sibling's successful slot, and a later conflicting incarnation cannot release an already successful slot. Creator bounds and an acyclic creation graph compose the instance factor. Relation-key bounds are separate and require a related type with no final state, with the sum taken over every connected sender/send. This excludes the native sibling-failure counterexample, the pre-failure related-item counterexample and repeatable transition creation. The checked native result implementation is packages/derive/src/delivery.ts285–290 (the note's scope/src pointer is a minor path typo, not a different runtime contract).\n\nThe previous pure probes remain distinguishing evidence for the premises, not a new package validator: sibling failure permits3 confirmed children through live max2, while own-item-only cleanup retains the two successful slots and refuses a third opening; a recycled max1 related item contributes2 keys; two nonfinal items per sender contribute2 keys. The revised design puts these in P1's negative/positive pairs and uses fan-in-exceeds-copies for a proved six-key bound above copies3, passing copies6. Unproved remains a different reason.\n\nGrow's positive case is now explicitly conditional on P1's source migration: Site.create-room conflict moves to a nonfinal conflicted state rather than failed; refused finalizes only its opening room. The Site's three successful-child slots then bound3 Room instances, while each Room's own nonfinal singleton bounds1 relation key. This approval does not claim the unchanged current Grow definition already satisfies that new rule. P1 owns the migration and the owning-slot, sibling-failure and conflict controls. Its real native result/replay and existing fault/closure cases must remain correct through that change.\n\nEarlier findings remain resolved: authenticated create-result/genesis endpoint writers and mutable result-assigned slots; under as a name and from.pin as the separately implemented digest check; singleton states with a named subject; supported-form staging and distinct refusal/warning/report witnesses; mandatory late bound/reason, branch-versus-refusal, strict boundary and dispatch→spacing→late→guards; S1 owns late/P2 spacing; stopped resolved members remain behind rather than falsely absent. Sequenced time/identity behavior follows the separately approved order design's prospective commit context and frozen prepare judgment time.\n\nEvidence limits: This is design approval only. No source/tests changed at this head, so docs/testing.md's documentation-only exception applies and no whole gate or mutation sweep was run. The pure validators/judges/folds probes use TEST in-memory authority/scripted founding, not validatePackage/from.pin/native-storage/provider acceptance. P1 and later slices still owe bounded implementation, native authority/replay, exact result-subject controls, Grow migration, scenario expectations independent of the manifest, actual install refusal and measured cost. Structural validation does not prove business correctness, cycle performance or outside effects. No provider, deployment, publication, actual-device, hostile-code isolation or completed G1/G2 claim.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a97343a2c958045a4dad0dfcec17236395e0a8f0","binding":"assigned","head":"44374d29f2f1f5e5f6e3417d35ac3d1a43279d54","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:efe2c298456fdef325703a3adc0ee6e55bd7ad27\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:751293b0cd462200f7822631fe9f2e227846278b\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:efe2c298456fdef325703a3adc0ee6e55bd7ad27","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}